# Mend Unified Agent configuration for the symfony real-world probe.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS -- it is aimed at the Dev Platform envs (ghc_*_dp).
# DP tenants do not read .whitesource at all; instead the framework reads this
# file and PUTs it as the tenant's UA config. When the file is absent the PUT is
# skipped entirely ("Skipping UA config PUT -- no whitesource.config in repo")
# and the scan runs on the platform's stored defaults.
#
# For this probe that was fatal: symfony ships composer.json with NO
# composer.lock, so Composer resolution needs the install pre-step. The DP
# default left it off and the scan resolved ZERO php dependencies -- silently,
# with no partialScanError and no scaResults error (totalFail:{}). Only the
# html/archive artifacts survived: 6 direct, 0 transitive, against the 21
# packages composer.json declares.
#
# .whitesource deliberately stays on configMode AUTO, so the classic envs
# (ghc_dev, ghc_staging, ghe) keep ignoring this file and their behaviour is
# unchanged. The values below mirror what those envs already produce.
php.resolveDependencies=true
php.runPreStep=true
php.includeDevDependencies=false
php.removeDuplicateDependencies=true
php.ignoreSourceFiles=true
